 	   	  		<h2 class="message">Archive for the &#8216;Botswana Travel&#8217; Category:</h2>
 	  
		        
        <div class="post" id="post-61">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-timeline/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Botswana Timeline">Botswana Timeline</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-timeline/#respond" title="Comment on Botswana Timeline">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content"> The Boer trekkers from the Transvaal were involved in various cattle and land wars with the local people, and great instability and militancy in Zululand - known as the period of the Difaqane (exodus) - forced many more groups ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-timeline/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Botswana Timeline">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-60">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/travelling-in-botswana/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Travelling in Botswana">Travelling in Botswana</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/travelling-in-botswana/#respond" title="Comment on Travelling in Botswana">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">Travelling in Botswana brings many joys. One that is always particularly pleasing is the visibility of the country's success. The rewards are on display, often highlighted in both urban and rural settings, as the old and traditional are juxtaposed with ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/travelling-in-botswana/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Travelling in Botswana">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-59">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/sir-seretse-khamas-leadership/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Sir Seretse Khama&#8217;s leadership">Sir Seretse Khama&#8217;s leadership</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/sir-seretse-khamas-leadership/#respond" title="Comment on Sir Seretse Khama&#8217;s leadership">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">Sir Seretse Khama was a visionary leafier - this plaque honouring him appears in the public garden at Jwaneng.
Although some still don't believe it, the country's major asset is its almost unparalleled wildlife resources and the selection of near pristine ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/sir-seretse-khamas-leadership/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Sir Seretse Khama&#8217;s leadership">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-58">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-in-the-70s/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Botswana in the 70&#8217;s">Botswana in the 70&#8217;s</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-in-the-70s/#respond" title="Comment on Botswana in the 70&#8217;s">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">Remember that, in the 1970s, Botswana was ranked as one of the world's poorest countries with a GDP per capita below US$ 200 and no economy to speak of, other than a fledgling beef industry that survived only because of ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/botswana-in-the-70s/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Botswana in the 70&#8217;s">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-57">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/gaborone-city-gabs/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Gaborone City &#8211; Gabs">Gaborone City &#8211; Gabs</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/gaborone-city-gabs/#respond" title="Comment on Gaborone City &#8211; Gabs">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
      Tags : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/batsalo-books/" rel="tag">Batsalo Books</a>, <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/bull-and-bush/" rel="tag">Bull and Bush</a>, <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/gabs-city/" rel="tag">Gabs City</a>, <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/game-city/" rel="tag">Game City</a>, <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/mugg-bean/" rel="tag">Mugg &amp; Bean</a>, <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/river-walk/" rel="tag">River walk</a><br /> Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">Gaborone, or Gabs City as the locals call it, is one of the world's fastest-growing metropolitan areas. While it only attained city status in 1986, phenomenal growth has seen it turn from a dusty backwater town into one of the ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/gaborone-city-gabs/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Gaborone City &#8211; Gabs">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-56">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/mokolodi-nature-reserve/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to MOKOLODI NATURE RESERVE">MOKOLODI NATURE RESERVE</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/mokolodi-nature-reserve/#respond" title="Comment on MOKOLODI NATURE RESERVE">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">No matter your reason for being in the capital city, if there is only one thing you do, make sure it is to visit this private nature reserve. Situated a mere 10 kilometres beyond the outskirts of Gaborone, it offers ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/mokolodi-nature-reserve/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to MOKOLODI NATURE RESERVE">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-55">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/kgalagadi-transfrontier-park/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to KGALAGADI TRANSFRONTIER PARK">KGALAGADI TRANSFRONTIER PARK</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/kgalagadi-transfrontier-park/#respond" title="Comment on KGALAGADI TRANSFRONTIER PARK">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">Incorporating the former Gemsbok National Park, this vast tract of semi-arid wilderness was Africa's first transfrontier park. It offers visitors an amazing variety of bird and animal life, and, if you're travelling in summer, you'll find that the rains can ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/kgalagadi-transfrontier-park/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to KGALAGADI TRANSFRONTIER PARK">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-54">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-remoteness-of-the-central-kalahari/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to THE REMOTENESS OF THE CENTRAL KALAHARI">THE REMOTENESS OF THE CENTRAL KALAHARI</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-remoteness-of-the-central-kalahari/#respond" title="Comment on THE REMOTENESS OF THE CENTRAL KALAHARI">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
      Tags : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/central-kalahari/" rel="tag">Central Kalahari</a><br /> Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">If
you want to escape totally the presence of others and the grind of everyday life, disappear somewhere deep into the Central Kalahari. With population dens¬ities amongst the lowest in the world, any one of the four reserves and game parks ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-remoteness-of-the-central-kalahari/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to THE REMOTENESS OF THE CENTRAL KALAHARI">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-53">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/a-sunset-cruise-on-the-chobe-river/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to A SUNSET CRUISE ON THE CHOBE RIVER">A SUNSET CRUISE ON THE CHOBE RIVER</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/a-sunset-cruise-on-the-chobe-river/#respond" title="Comment on A SUNSET CRUISE ON THE CHOBE RIVER">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
      Tags : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/tag/chobe-safari-lodge/" rel="tag">Chobe Safari Lodge</a><br /> Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">The Chobe National Park is world renowned for its prolific elephant population, and a sunset cruise, particularly in the winter months, is a great way to make their acquaintance. Chobe Chilwero offers an exclusive option away from the crush, while ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/a-sunset-cruise-on-the-chobe-river/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to A SUNSET CRUISE ON THE CHOBE RIVER">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
        <div class="post" id="post-52">
        
        <h2><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-moremisavutichobe-self-drive/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to THE MOREMI/SAVUTI/CHOBE SELF-DRIVE">THE MOREMI/SAVUTI/CHOBE SELF-DRIVE</a></h2>
        <div class="date">{ Posted on Jan 02 2010 by admin }<div class="comms"><a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-moremisavutichobe-self-drive/#respond" title="Comment on THE MOREMI/SAVUTI/CHOBE SELF-DRIVE">No Comments</a></div></div>
        
        
        <div class="meta">
       Categories : <a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/category/travel-to-botswana/" title="View all posts in Botswana Travel" rel="category tag">Botswana Travel</a>         </div><!--meta-->
        
        <div class="content">The
continent's most popular self-drive safari route takes in the south-eastern fringes of the Okavango Delta and two of Africa's finest game parks, Moremi and Chobe. It's the real deal with no frills attached, and for the self- drive devotee it ...<a href="http://www.botswanasite.com/the-moremisavutichobe-self-drive/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to THE MOREMI/SAVUTI/CHOBE SELF-DRIVE">Read More &raquo;</a></div>
        
        </div><!--post-->
        
                        
